Hi All,<br><br>Really liking this project. I have managed to get everything up and<br>running, and can run the test provided in the documentation. So I<br>wanted to run a simple example of loading a file, reading the file<br>into R and then doing some stuff on the data therein.<br><br>However, I get an error message that the directory doesn&#39;t exist. I am<br>running Apache as a regular user (actually using my own userID), and I<br>have permissions to create directories and files in /tmp, so I&#39;m not<br>sure what is going on. Should I be somehow copying the file somewhere<br>else before submitting to the function? From the documentation I<br>thought that the directory would exist for the duration of the<br>&#39;rhandler&#39;, which seems to me should mean my function should be able<br>to access it.<br><br>I would appreciate any suggestions as to how to proceed.<br><br>Cheers,<br><br>-Robert<br><br>Function:<br><br>summaryOut &lt;- function(FILES){<br>	if (!is.null(FILES)){<br><br>		fileName &lt;- paste(FILES$file1$tmp_name,FILES$file1$name,sep=&quot;/&quot;)<br>		dt &lt;- matrix(scan(fileName,skip=1), ncol=3)<br><br>		meanDT &lt;- apply(dt,2,mean)<br>		sdDT &lt;- apply(dt,2,sd)<br>		cat(&#39;mean &#39;, meanDT, &#39;&lt;br&gt;&#39;)<br>		cat(&#39;sd &#39;, sdDT, &#39;&lt;br&gt;&#39;)<br>	}<br>	else {<br>		cat(&#39;No file entered!&#39;)<br>	}<br>}<br><br>setContentType(&quot;text/html&quot;)<br><br>cat(&#39;&lt;HTML&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;BODY&gt;
